Zune68k lean [RELEASE] for AmigaOS 3.x / m68k
=============================================

Zune68k lean is a muimaster.library for AmigaOS 3.x: AROS's Zune as
ported to AmigaOS 3 by Zune68 (Stefan Reinauer), with a diet so that it
runs on a stock 68000 with OS 3.1 and stays close to MUI 3.8 in memory.
This is a test build ([STAGE], [RELEASE]). The figures here were
measured in an emulator (FS-UAE), not on a real Amiga.

Requirements
------------
AmigaOS 3.1 or newer, a 68000 or better, no FPU. Amiga Installer 43 or
newer: OS 3.2 has SYS:System/Installer; for OS 3.1 use Installer 43.3
(Aminet util/misc; the Installer on the OS 3.1 Install disk is older).
The Install icon's default tool is "installer"; if Workbench cannot find
it, set the icon's Default Tool to its full path.

Installing
----------
Double-click Install, or from a Shell in this drawer:

  Installer Install MINUSER AVERAGE

The installer first shows what it found: a MUI you already have (MUI 3.x,
4 or 5 in SYS:MUI or MUI:, its lines in S:User-Startup), every
muimaster.library in the LIBS: drawers, and an earlier Zune. None of it
is changed. Zune goes into the first LIBS: drawer (normally SYS:Libs),
which programs search before MUI's MUI:Libs, so they get Zune; nothing is
added to S:Startup-Sequence or S:User-Startup.

  Libs/muimaster.library, zunemaster.library -> first LIBS: drawer
  Libs/Zune/*        -> LIBS:Zune/ (Zune's own class files and modules,
                        loaded when a program first needs them)
  Libs/MUI/*         -> LIBS:MUI/ of the first LIBS: drawer, never into
                        MUI's own MUI:Libs/mui
  Prefs/Zune         -> SYS:Prefs/Zune
  Locale/Catalogs/*  -> LOCALE:Catalogs/<language>/ (optional)
  Tools/ZuneSwitch and the icons below -> SYS:Zune68k

Every file the installer replaces is kept in SYS:Zune68k/Data/Backup, and
every file it installs is written down in SYS:Zune68k/Data/Manifest.

The bundled MUI classes (NList, TextEditor, TheBar, ...): one is installed
only when you have no same or newer version of it in a LIBS:MUI drawer; an
older one of yours is kept in the backup. The classes that come with a
real MUI (in MUI:Libs/mui) belong to that MUI and are not used by Zune:
Zune gets its own copy, and the real MUI gets its own back with "Use real
MUI". The last page of the installer lists what it did with each.

Running Install again offers "Install this version over it" (an update:
the earlier installation is removed first, your files put back, then this
one installed; your Zune settings are kept) and "Remove Zune68k".

Novice installs everything without questions; Intermediate and Expert
ask whether to install the translations. Pretend mode changes nothing.

Use real MUI, Use Zune, Uninstall
---------------------------------
In SYS:Zune68k (Use real MUI and Use Zune only when a real MUI was
found):

  Use real MUI  puts Zune's libraries and classes aside (into
                SYS:Zune68k/Data/Parked) and your own files they had
                replaced back. After a reboot programs get your MUI.
  Use Zune      the other way round, after a reboot programs get Zune.
  Uninstall     deletes every file Zune installed, puts back every file
                of yours it had replaced, and removes the drawers it made
                when they are empty. Asks whether to keep your Zune
                settings (ENVARC:Zune). Your MUI keeps working.

From a Shell: SYS:Zune68k/Data/ZuneSwitch MUI, ZUNE, UNINSTALL [SETTINGS]
or STATUS (what is installed where).

Settings
--------
SYS:Prefs/Zune, the Zune preferences program. MUI's own settings
(ENVARC:MUI) are not read or changed by Zune.

Each program gets the MUI it asks for: a program written for MUI 3 sees
MUI 3.8 (muimaster.library 19.35), one asking for MUI 4 sees MUI 4, one
asking for MUI 5 sees MUI 5 (21.227), and Zune follows the same choice.
Zune prefs, System page, "MUI version": "Behave as" Automatic (the
default), MUI 3.8, MUI 4 or MUI 5 for all programs, and a list of
programs (by file name) with a MUI of their own. Many programs written
for MUI 4/5 ask for 19 and so get MUI 3.8 under Automatic: give such a
program MUI 5 in that list.

Status
------
A test build of muimaster.library [VERSION], dated [RELEASE].
In FS-UAE (A1200, OS 3.1, 68000 build): MUI 3.8's 19 demos open and close
with MUI 3.8's window sizes, 18 of 27 demo windows pixel for pixel as MUI
3.8's; of 36 MUI 3 programs, 30 behave as with MUI 3.8 (see
Compatibility). MUI-Demo with 4 MB fast RAM: about 465 KB for the first
program (MUI 3.8: 460 KB), about 205 KB for each further one (MUI 3.8:
211-219 KB), first window 1.4 s (MUI 3.8: 1.5 s). Not yet measured on a
real Amiga. Please report what works and what does not, with the
program's version, your CPU and OS.

Developing with the SDK
-----------------------
Add SDK/include to the include path and link with -lmui:

  m68k-amigaos-gcc -noixemul -Os -I../include -o HelloZune HelloZune.c -lmui

